Subject: [PATCH] compositor: avoid shader app-window layer on Watch3 R08

The pinned AsteroidOS compositor's WindowWrapperBase still applies a
CircleMaskShader layer when gesture-driven app-window borders are smoothed.
Qt Quick's software backend cannot render ShaderEffect layers, so removing
only the fullscreen corner mask is not sufficient. The R08 physical watch
panel already has circular edges.

Keep this change R08-specific in meta-noblesse and preserve upstream
behavior for machines using GPU-backed scenegraphs. No hardware display
or Wayland runtime validation has been performed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff --git a/src/qml/compositor/WindowWrapperBase.qml b/src/qml/compositor/WindowWrapperBase.qml
--- a/src/qml/compositor/WindowWrapperBase.qml
+++ b/src/qml/compositor/WindowWrapperBase.qml
@@ -59,6 +59,6 @@
         window.y = 0
     }
 
-    layer.enabled: smoothBorders && DeviceSpecs.hasRoundScreen
-    layer.effect: CircleMaskShader { }
+    // R08: the physical round display already clips application windows.
+    // Avoid the unsupported GPU shader layer on the Qt Quick software backend.
 }
